"[2510.13331v1] Group-Wise Optimization for Self-Extensible Codebooks in Vector Quantized Models (https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.13331v1)\nciteturn3048view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 6 months ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.13331v1\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 202\nL0: cite0†Skip to main content L1: \nL2:  cite57†Image: Cornell University L3: \nL4: cite1†Learn about arXiv becoming an independent nonprofit.†tech.cornell.edu L5: \nL6:  We gratefully acknowledge support from the Simons Foundation, cite2†member institutions†info.arxiv.org , and all contributors. cite3†Donate†info.arxiv.org L7: \nL8: cite58†Image: arxiv logo > cite4†cs > arXiv:2510.13331v1\nL9: \nL10: cite5†Help†info.arxiv.org | cite6†Advanced Search L11:  All fields Title Author Abstract Comments Journal reference ACM classification MSC classification Report number arXiv identifier DOI ORCID arXiv author ID Help pages Full text\nL12: \nL13: Search\nL14: \nL15: cite59†Image: arXiv logo L16: \nL17: cite7† †www.cornell.edu L18: \nL19:  open search\nL20: \nL21: GO\nL22: \nL23: open navigation menu\nL24: ## quick links\nL25: \nL26:   * cite8†Login L27:   * cite5†Help Pages†info.arxiv.org L28:   * cite9†About†info.arxiv.org L29: \nL30: # Computer Science > Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition\nL31: \nL32: arXiv:2510.13331v1 (cs)\nL33: \nL34: [Submitted on 15 Oct 2025 (this version), latest version 16 Oct 2025 (cite10†v2 )]\nL35: # Title:Group-Wise Optimization for Self-Extensible Codebooks in Vector Quantized Models\nL36: \nL37: Authors:cite11†Hong-Kai Zheng , cite12†Piji Li L38: \nL39: View a PDF of the paper titled Group-Wise Optimization for Self-Extensible Codebooks in Vector Quantized Models, by Hong-Kai Zheng and 1 other authors\nL40: \nL41: cite13†View PDF cite14†HTML (experimental) L42: > Abstract:Vector Quantized Variational Autoencoders (VQ-VAEs) leverage self-supervised learning through reconstruction tasks to represent continuous vectors using the closest vectors in a codebook. However, issues such as codebook collapse persist in the VQ model. To address these issues, existing approaches employ implicit static codebooks or jointly optimize the entire codebook, but these methods constrain the codebook's learning capability, leading to reduced reconstruction quality.\nL43: In this paper, we propose Group-VQ, which performs group-wise optimization on the codebook. Each group is optimized independently, with joint optimization performed within groups. This approach improves the trade-off between codebook utilization and reconstruction performance. Additionally, we introduce a training-free codebook resampling method, allowing post-training adjustment of the codebook size.\nL44: In image reconstruction experiments under various settings, Group-VQ demonstrates improved performance on reconstruction metrics. And the post-training codebook sampling method achieves the desired flexibility in adjusting the codebook size.\nL45: Subjects: Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (cs.CV)\nL46: Cite as: cite15†arXiv:2510.13331 [cs.CV]\nL47:   (or  cite16†arXiv:2510.13331v1 [cs.CV] for this version)\nL48:   cite17†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2510.13331†doi.org L49: \nL50: Focus to learn more\nL51: \nL52:   arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL53: ## Submission history\nL54: \nL55: From: Hong-Kai Zheng [cite18†view email ]\nL56: [v1] Wed, 15 Oct 2025 09:14:22 UTC (1,518 KB)\nL57: cite10†[v2] Thu, 16 Oct 2025 05:26:09 UTC (1,483 KB)\nL58: \nL59: Full-text links:\nL60: ## Access Paper:\nL61: \nL62:  View a PDF of the paper titled Group-Wise Optimization for Self-Extensible Codebooks in Vector Quantized Models, by Hong-Kai Zheng and 1 other authors\nL63: \nL64:   * cite13†View PDF L65:   * cite14†HTML (experimental) L66:   * cite19†TeX Source  L67: \nL68: cite20†view license L69: \nL70: Current browse context:\nL71: \nL72: cs.CV\nL73: \nL74: