ls and organizations that work with arXivLabs have embraced and accepted our values of openness, community, excellence, and user data privacy. arXiv is committed to these values and only works with partners that adhere to them.\nL152: Have an idea for a project that will add value for arXiv's community? cite39†Learn more about arXivLabs†info.arxiv.org .\nL153: \nL154: cite40†Which authors of this paper are endorsers? | Disable MathJax (cite41†What is MathJax?†info.arxiv.org )\nL155: \nL156: We gratefully acknowledge support from our major funders, cite42†member institutions†info.arxiv.org , , and all contributors.\nL157: cite43†About†info.arxiv.org · cite44†Help†info.arxiv.org · cite45†Contact†info.arxiv.org · cite46†Subscribe†info.arxiv.org · cite47†Copyright†info.arxiv.org · cite48†Privacy†info.arxiv.org · cite49†Accessibility†info.arxiv.org · cite50†Operational Status (opens in new tab)†status.arxiv.org L158: \nL159: Major funding support from\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n[2510.13454v1] VIST3A: Text-to-3D by Stitching a Multi-view Reconstruction Network to a Video Generator (https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.13454v1)\nciteturn3048view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 weeks ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.13454v1\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 162\nL0: cite0†Search cite1†Submit cite2†Donate†info.arxiv.org cite3†Log in L1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · cite4†Advanced search L5: \nL6: # Computer Science > Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 15 Oct 2025 (this version), latest version 5 Mar 2026 (cite5†v2 )]\nL9: # Title:VIST3A: Text-to-3D by Stitching a Multi-view Reconstruction Network to a Video Generator\nL10: \nL11: Authors:cite6†Hyojun Go , cite7†Dominik Narnhofer , cite8†Goutam Bhat , cite9†Prune Truong , cite10†Federico Tombari , cite11†Konrad Schindler L12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled VIST3A: Text-to-3D by Stitching a Multi-view Reconstruction Network to a Video Generator, by Hyojun Go and 5 other authors\nL14: \nL15: cite12†View PDF cite13†HTML (experimental) L16: > Abstract:The rapid progress of large, pretrained models for both visual content generation and 3D reconstruction opens up new possibilities for text-to-3D generation. Intuitively, one could obtain a formidable 3D scene generator if one were able to combine the power of a modern latent text-to-video model as \"generator\" with the geometric abilities of a recent (feedforward) 3D reconstruction system as \"decoder\". We introduce VIST3A, a general framework that does just that, addressing two main challenges.\nL17: First, the two components must be joined in a way that preserves the rich knowledge encoded in their weights. We revisit model stitching, i.e., we identify the layer in the 3D decoder that best matches the latent representation produced by the text-to-video generator and stitch the two parts together. That operation requires only a small dataset and no labels.\nL18: Second, the text-to-video generator must be aligned with the stitched 3D decoder, to ensure that the generated latents are decodable into consistent, perceptually convincing 3D scene geometry. To that end, we adapt direct reward finetuning, a popular technique for human preference alignment. We evaluate the proposed VIST3A approach with different video generators and 3D reconstruction models. All tested pairings markedly improve over prior text-to-3D models that output Gaussian splats.\nL19: Moreover, by choosing a suitable 3D base model, VIST3A also enables high-quality text-to-pointmap generation.\nL20: Comments:  | Project page: cite14†this https URL†gohyojun15.github.io L21: Subjects:  | Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (cs.CV)\nL22: Cite as:  | cite15†arXiv:2510.13454 [cs.CV]\nL23:    | (or cite16†arXiv:2510.13454v1 [cs.CV] for this version)\nL24:    | cite17†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2510.13454†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL25: ## Submission history\nL26: \nL27: From: Hyojun Go [cite18†view email ]\nL28: [v1] Wed, 15 Oct 2025 11:55:08 UTC (13,003 KB)\nL29: cite5†[v2] Thu, 5 Mar 2026 09:57:15 UTC (15,363 KB)\nL30: \nL31: Full-text links:\nL32: \nL33: ## Access Paper:\nL34: \nL35: View a PDF of the paper titled VIST3A: Text-to-3D by Stitching a Multi-view Reconstruction Network to a Video Generator, by Hyojun Go and 5 other authors\nL36: \nL37:   * cite12†View PDF L38:   * cite13†HTML (experimental) L39:   * cite19†TeX Source L40: \nL41: cite20†view license†creativecommons.org L42: ### Current browse context:\nL43: \nL44: cs.CV\nL45: \nL46: cite21†< prev |   cite22†next > L47: \nL48: cite23†new | cite24†recent | cite25†2025-10 L49: \nL50: Change to browse by:\nL51: \nL52: cite26†cs L53: \nL54: ### References & Citations\nL55: \nL56:   * cite27†NASA ADS†ui.adsabs.harvard.edu L57:   * cite28†Google Scholar†scholar.google.com L58:   * cite29†Semantic Scholar†api.semanticscholar.org L59: \nL60: [Button: export BibTeX citation] Loading...\nL61: \nL62: ## BibTeX formatted citation\nL63: \nL64: [Button: ×]\nL65: \nL66: loading...\nL67: \nL68: Data provided by:\nL69: \nL70: ### Bookmark\nL71: \nL72: [Input] Bibliographic Tools\nL73: # Bibliographic and Citation Tools\nL74: \nL75: [Input] Bibliographic Explorer Toggle\nL76: \nL77: Bibliographic Explorer (cite30†What is the Explorer?†info.arxiv.org )\nL78: \nL79: [Input] Connected Papers Toggle\nL80: \nL81: Connected Papers (cite31†What is Connected Papers?†www.connectedpapers.com )\nL82: \nL83: [Input] Litmaps Toggle\nL84: \nL85: Litmaps (cite32†What is Litmaps?†www.litmaps.co )\nL86: \nL87: [Input] scite.ai Toggle\nL88: \nL89: scite Smart Citations (cite33†What are Smart Citations?†www.scite.ai )\nL90: